months after the initiation of insulin therapy, he presented w ith
abdominal stiﬀness, painful spasms extending to lower limbs,
and impaired walking ability. Neurological examination sho wed
muscle rigidity and bilateral contractures in the lower lim bs but
no muscular weakness. Electroencephalography was normal,
and electromyography/nerve conduction velocity revealed
slightly asymmetrical motor and sensory polyneuropathy with
demyelination. These features were highly indicative of SP S.
